\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa319\sl276\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9712292 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid9712292\charrsid9712292 \hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 
The development of financial sentiment analysis reflects the shift in natural language processing from rule-based, symbolic methods to neural network-based contextual language models. Early approaches used domain-specific sentiment lexicons to identify po
\hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 larity-related terms in financial texts. Loughran and McDonald (2011) demonstrated that general sentiment dictionaries have low accuracy }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid9712292 \hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 
in}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid9712292\charrsid9712292 \hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0  financial writing\hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid9712292 \hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 because}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid9712292\charrsid9712292 \hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 \hich\f0  words like \'93\loch\f0 \hich\f0 liability\'94\loch\f0 
 have different meanings in finance than in everyday English. Their finance-specific lexicon fixed this problem and set a benchmark for future research in computational finance.
\par \hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 
The advent of transformer-based models marked a major change in financial sentiment analysis. For example, Araci (2019) introduced FinBERT, a BERT model fine-tuned on financial news and reports, which improved accuracy by 15% compared to earlier methods. 
\hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 FinBERT also proved effective with limited labeled data,\hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 
 outperforming baseline models trained on as few as 500 samples. This showed that transfer learning is useful for financial NLP tasks with small datasets.
\par \hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 Mishev et al. (2020) c}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid9712292 \hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 onducted}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid9712292\charrsid9712292 \hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 
 over 100 experiments to systematically compare \hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 sentiment analysis methods, }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid9712292 \hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 ranging }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f0\fs24\insrsid9712292\charrsid9712292 \hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 
from lexicons to transformers. Their comprehensive study tested BERT variants, including RoBERTa, XLNet, ALBERT, and DistilBERT, on several financial datasets. They found that contextual embeddings are much more effective than lexicons and fixed-word enco
\hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 ders. BERT and ALBERT-xxlarge achieved the highest scores, with }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid9712292 \hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 a }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid9712292\charrsid9712292 
\hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 Matthews Correlation Coefficient of 0.895 and 0.881, respectively. Importantly, distilled transformers like DistilBERT kept over 95% of BERT\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 
s accuracy while using 40% fewer parameters, making them suitable for production environments with limited computi\hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 ng power.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid9712292 
