The use of sentiment analysis for regime detection remains an emerging area with significant untapped potential. Foundational research has shown that sentiment signals can predict market movements: 
\par \hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 
Bollen et al. (2011) found that Twitter mood states predicted DJIA movements 2-6 days in advance with 86.7% accuracy (87.6% in direction), indicating sentiment as a possible leading indicator. Their analysis highlighted specific emotional dimensions (calm
\hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0  and anxiety) linked to subsequent market movements, implying that changes in investor psychology often precede price shifts. 
\par \hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 
Renault (2017) built a specialized sentiment lexicon from StockTwits messages and studied intraday links between sentiment and returns of the S&P 500 ETF. The results showed that sentiment changes in the first half-hour predicted returns in the last half-
\hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 hour, mainly influenced by novice traders. A trading strategy based on this pattern achieved a Sharpe ratio of 1.496 and significant price reversals the next trading day\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 
aligning with noise-trading theory. Crucially, this predictability disappeared when u\hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 si\hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 ng standard dictionary-based sentiment methods, emphasizing the importance of domain-specific lexicons. 

\par \hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 Micaletti (2022) proposed the idea of relative sentiment\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 the gap between institutional and individual investor expectations\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 
for tactical asset allocation. Using Sentix economic sentiment indices across the U.S., Europe, Japan, and Asia ex-Japan, he discov\hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 
ered that relative sentiment factors had strong predictive power across all regions, outperforming both standalone sentiment and time-series momentum in informational value. Combined relative sentiment strategies outperformed benchmarks by 400-700 basis p
\hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 oi\hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 nts annually, with higher Sharpe ratios and lower maximum drawdowns. Notably, when time-series momentum was negative,\hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 
 but relative sentiment was positive, annualized returns averaged 27%, compared to -23% when both were negative\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 a 50-percentage-point difference driven by sentiment state}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
