Blob, and RoBERTa, their model captured both cross-sectional asset dependencies and temporal dynamics. The approach improved forecast accuracy by 1.02% over a 1-day horizon, 0.42% over 20 days, and 0.36% over 50 days compared with LSTM, Random Forest, and
\hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0  R\hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 
NN models. A key practical insight was that while RoBERTa-based sentiment extraction was more accurate, it increased computational costs from 3-6 seconds (for simpler methods) to as much as 14 hours, emphasizing the trade-off between accuracy and real-tim
\hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 e application. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid1668116 
