The structure of sentiment predictability naturally follows a hierarchy: immediate sentiment changes (intraday) generate noise trading signals; short-term aggregation (1-5 days) captures momentum; and medium-term patterns (weekly to monthly) may indicate 
\hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 regime-level shifts. Our proposed framework aims at detecting these medium-term regimes while maintaining responsiveness to rapid sentiment downturns during crises.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 
