The previous literature review identifies several key gaps that drive our research approach. First, while sentiment analysis has shown strong performance for individual asset classes, there is no framework that systematically combines sentiment across equ
\hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 
ities, cryptocurrencies, forex, and commodities to identify regime shifts at the portfolio level. Second, although evidence indicates that sentiment signals can predict price movements 1-6 days in advance, this lead time has not been utilized for regime-l
\hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 ev\hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 
el early warning systems. Third, network-based methods have highlighted the importance of sentiment connectedness, yet cross-asset sentiment networks are still unexplored. Fourth, the practical integration of multi-source sentiment data (such as social me
\hich\af0\dbch\af31501\loch\f0 dia, news, and financial reports) with regime detection algorithms has not yet been attempted.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs24\insrsid10292334\charrsid1668116 
